= Exploratory Data Analysis

This analysis looks at the Smoke-Fire Detection Dataset@smoke_fire_yolo, which is designed for training and evaluating YOLO-based object detection models. The dataset contains over 20,000 images showing a variety of enviroments and scenarios, including scenes containig, smoke, fire, both or neither. Some images represent a sequence of observations of the same scene, while others cpature identical locations at different points in time. The dataset combines images from multiple publically available datasets into a single colleciton, giving a diverse range of scenarios for fire and smoke detection.

The analysis follows as:

+ Examine the distribution of samples
+ Bounding-box properties for fire/smoke 
+ Image level statistics (brightness, contrast, etc.)
+ Correlation between features of the dataset 